{"review":{"at":"2026-11-09T17:40:19-06:00","size":"full","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"The new test is unindexed: `Servex/agents/map.md:55` lists every `*.test.mjs` in the folder (`item-read.test.mjs`, `item_tool.test.mjs`, …), but not `item-verbs.test.mjs`. Add it there (Law 10). `Servex/doc/item-tool.md` already names it."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"The task log is stale, so a fresh agent would be misled. `item-verbs/session.jsonl` ends with \"Landed … (11 checks) … Commit 1e93b29d4\", but the branch `worktree/item-verbs` also has a later commit, 500732cc3 (session 7caa4528: dotted `set` keys are checked at their last step). That commit has no log line, and the test now runs 12 checks. Add a log line naming 500732cc3, and make clear the merge must take both commits."},{"n":3,"kind":"note","text":"The brief named the test file `Servex/agents/item_tool.test.mjs`, but that file already exists (148 checks), so the work went into a new `item-verbs.test.mjs`. That is the right call, but neither the task log nor the commit says so."},{"n":4,"kind":"note","text":"Schema copies: there is only one. The `local` MCP (`item-local.test.mjs`) and RemoteMCP (`RemoteMCP.test.mjs:20`) both register `page_tools()`, so the new params reach every door. `git grep ITEM_DESCRIPTION` finds only `page_tools.js`. The minion's report should have said this explicitly instead of leaving it to the reader."},{"n":5,"kind":"note","text":"`ITEM_DESCRIPTION` (`page_tools.js:467`) still opens with \"`item({path, delta})`\" and only then says \"Prefer the verbs\". To match the brief's \"one sentence at the front\", lead with `item({path, get|set|call})`."},{"n":6,"kind":"note","text":"The `args` param (`page_tools.js` schema, `args:`) has no `type`. That is valid JSON Schema (any value), but it is the only untyped property among the tool's parameters. Worth a look if a client validator complains."},{"n":7,"kind":"note","text":"The `call` query refusal reads `owner?.queries` from the constructor of the node the path reaches. For a List (e.g. `call: \"tasks.summary\"`), that is List's own `queries` (probably none), so a list-level query would fall through to the \"not a method\" refusal. Nothing is written either way, but the refusal names the wrong fix."}],"branch":"worktree/item-verbs","head":"500732cc33caa1c9d457581ff56cc00c6e222ceb","model":"claude-opus-5-5","cost":0.9700454000000001,"file":"review.md","report":null,"shots":null}}
